.el .ds Aq '
.TH snip-theme 1 "" "snip 0.6.0" "Snip Manual"
.SH "NAME"
snip\-theme \- inspect and manage TUI color themes
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBsnip theme\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
\fBsnip theme list\fR [\fB\-\-appearance\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
\fBsnip theme show\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
\fBsnip theme check\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
\fBsnip theme path\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
\fBsnip theme export\fR [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
\fBsnip theme import\fR [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-syntax\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPATH\fR> 
\fBsnip theme use\fR [\fB\-\-appearance\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
List, inspect, validate, export, import, and select TUI color themes. Built\-in and user themes share the same validation rules. Appearance slots allow separate light and dark choices.
.PP
export copies a theme into the user theme directory for editing. import converts a base16 or base24 scheme. check reports contrast and role\-distinctness problems before a theme is selected.
.PP
Global options are described in snip(1).
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "snip theme"
List, inspect, and switch TUI color themes
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS "snip theme list"
List available themes
.TP
\fB\-\-appearance\fR \fI<APPEARANCE>\fR
Restrict to one appearance
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS "snip theme show"
Print one theme's resolved colors
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Theme name
.SS "snip theme check"
Validate a theme's contrast and role distinctness
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Theme name
.SS "snip theme path"
Print the directory user themes are read from
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS "snip theme export"
Write a theme to the user theme directory so it can be edited
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<AS>\fR
Name to save it under. Defaults to "<name>\-custom"
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite an existing exported theme
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Theme name to export
.SS "snip theme import"
Convert a base16 scheme file into a user theme
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<AS>\fR
Name to save it under. Defaults to the file stem
.TP
\fB\-\-syntax\fR \fI<SYNTAX>\fR
Use an embedded syntax theme instead of deriving one from the palette
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite an existing theme file
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Convert and print the theme without writing anything
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
Path to a base16 or base24 scheme file, or "\-" to read stdin
.SS "snip theme use"
Select a theme for its appearance slot and save it to the config
.TP
\fB\-\-appearance\fR \fI<APPEARANCE>\fR
Write to this slot instead of the theme\*(Aqs own appearance
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Theme name to select
.SH "EXAMPLES"
List dark themes and inspect one as JSON:
.RS 4
.nf
snip theme list \-\-appearance dark
snip \-\-output json theme show dracula
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export a theme for editing and validate the result:
.RS 4
.nf
snip theme export dracula \-\-as dracula\-custom
snip theme check dracula\-custom
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR snip (1),
.BR snip\-tui (1),
.BR snip\-config (1),
.BR snip\-theme (5)
